cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Auto_Sernamont: automated Sénarmont polarimetry for electro-optic and
  ferroelectric mapping of BaTiO3 thin films
message: >-
  If you use this software or its analysis in your work, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bickerdike
    given-names: Adam
repository-code: 'https://github.com/adambickerdike/Auto_Sernamont'
abstract: >-
  An instrument-control and analysis system for measuring the linear
  electro-optic (Pockels) response and the ferroelectric switching behaviour of
  a 10x10 electrode array on a barium titanate thin film at 1550 nm. It drives
  three motorised polarisation optics, a two-axis translation stage, a
  100-channel electrode switching matrix, a source-measure unit, a function
  generator, an oscilloscope and a lock-in amplifier, and turns the acquired
  phasors into normalised electro-optic rotations, angular certificates,
  hysteresis-loop metrics and chip-level maps.
keywords:
  - electro-optics
  - Pockels effect
  - barium titanate
  - ferroelectrics
  - polarimetry
  - Senarmont
  - lock-in detection
  - laboratory automation
  - photonics
license: MIT
